#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188043 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "ea6a79c4-09fc-5ae9-9e92-e7bacd4939d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10340" :question/problem "${3x^{2},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X \\, & \\, Y=-2\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, -2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{X \\mid -2}=\\dfrac{3}{4}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(X - μ_{X \\mid y})^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{X \\mid y}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X^2 \\, & \\, Y=y \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x^2 \\, f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}x^{2}f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}x^{2} \\cdot 3x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}3x^{4}dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{3x^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5} - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{X \\mid - 2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5} - (\\frac{3}{4})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5} - \\frac{9}{16} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{80}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188044 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "fef21fcb-bab6-5f33-a792-280e28a97f81" :question/math-academy-id "e-10341" :question/problem "${\\frac{3}{y^{4}},\\begin{vmatrix}y \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=3\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 3)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{Y \\mid 3}=\\dfrac{3}{2}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 3\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 3)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{∞}y^{2} \\cdot \\frac{3}{y^{4}}dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{∞}\\frac{3}{y^{2}}dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{∞}3y^{-2}dy \\\\\n&= [3 \\cdot (y^{-1})/((-1))]_{1}^{∞} \\\\\n&= [- \\frac{3}{y}]_{1}^{∞} \\\\\n&= 0 - (-3) \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 3\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 3\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid 3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3 - (\\frac{3}{2})^{2} \\\\\n&= 3 - \\frac{9}{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188045 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "acb4923c-ce04-5cd5-af01-2f078a18ceed" :question/math-academy-id "e-10342" :question/problem "$f(x, y) = {2y\\ln (x),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le e, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwisef_{X}(x) = {\\ln (x),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le e, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\,\\big & \\, X=1 \\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{Y \\mid 1}=\\dfrac{2}{3}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X = x \\big\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$.\n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x) &= (f(x, y))/(f_{X}(x)) \\\\\n&= (2y\\ln (x))/(\\ln (x)) \\\\\n&= 2y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n1 \\leq x \\leq e, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nOutside this domain, we have\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\mid X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x) = 0\n$$\n\nNotice that $f_{Y \\mid X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ does not depend on $x$. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 1)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}y^{2} \\cdot 2ydy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}2y^{3}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{4}}{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid 1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} - (\\frac{2}{3})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{4}{9} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820466ba-6f36-5d47-afef-0ee20288f099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186625} {:answer/id #uuid "a4fa1bcc-91b5-57e8-85ba-c02fe35e14e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186626} {:answer/id #uuid "cb641e71-4763-57b7-bdbf-54ac5c041138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186627} {:answer/id #uuid "f74163e9-f3d4-5fad-816e-1c659459e6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186628} {:answer/id #uuid "08a51dff-0f49-52c1-ab38-9208cc65b517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186629}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2338bb54-2402-5bab-b83e-832eb2b270cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186624}] :question/id #uuid "3cefc73e-1ad2-58be-a1de-e39c1b293d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-146806" :question/problem "$f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2) = {\\frac{4}{x^{5}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional variance $Var\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $μ_{X \\mid - 2} = \\frac{4}{3}$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
